      "math_academy_id": "q-140114",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 8+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 10+2\\cdot 6}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{8+4-10+12}{1+1+1+4}b \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{7}b \\\\  & =2b \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
